    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nSeveral Vim-owned ftplugins source other ftplugins through an explicit `.vim` runtime lookup. For example, `ftplugin/gitsendemail.vim` contains:\n\n```\nruntime! ftplugin/mail.vim\n```\n\nThis skips any corresponding Lua ftplugin (here `mail.lua`). This issue applies to a large number of ftplugins. One (and only?) exception is `runtime/ftplugin/cpp.vim`, which includes both Vimscript and Lua files:\n\n```\nruntime! ftplugin/c[.]{vim,lua} ftplugin/c_*.{vim,lua} ftplugin/c/*.{vim,lua}\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nA general solution or convention for sourcing corresponding Lua ftplugins seems needed. One option might be to add matching Lua ftplugins for these cases? For example, `ftplugin/gitsendemail.lua` could source `ftplugin/mail.lua` alongside the existing Vimscript dependency.",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-13T22:18:52Z",
