    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This issue is more accurately named as:\n\nVimscript ftplugins that source base ftplugins skip corresponding Lua ftplugins\n\nbut I don't have perms to change it.\n\nAfter looking through, this occurs _all the time_ in neovim plugins. For example, objc.vim SKIPS c.lua. This is not intuitive. I see three ways forward:\n\n1. alter all ftplugins to be lua-aware, like the cpp.vim pattern above\n2. create nvim-only lua ftplugin shims (i.e. gitsendemail.lua) which will auto-source the corresponding nested lua ftplugins\n3. convert builtin ftplugins to lua\n\n@clason I know you know the trade-offs of these approaches already... interested in your thoughts here",
            "created_at": "2026-07-13T18:18:24Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/40709#issuecomment-4961184125",
