        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I don't think option 3 pays off: that would prevent us from easily merging upstream changes.\n\nOption 2 is the least intrusive and most explicit (and simplest), although that would lead to a different ordering that may be observable. (There's a reason why the c ftplugin is the way it is.)\n\nThe secret option 4 is to change `:runtime foo` (without extension) to transparently source both vimscript and Lua files (\"Do What I Mean(tm)\"), but that is of course more involved (but would help plugins not have to worry about Lua).\n\n(There's a related todo(clason) about the Nvim API not supporting proper ordering; can't dig it up on mobile right now.)\n\nSo option 1 sounds easiest (and easy to revert later in favor of option 4 or friends.)",
            "created_at": "2026-07-13T18:32:01Z",
